// It exists because a gRPC error alone cannot express it. Every SIEM destination
// can answer HTTP 200 and still refuse the payload, and the distinction between
// "refused deterministically" and "temporarily unavailable" decides whether the
// host retries — for OTLP the specification forbids retrying a partial success
// outright. Without a response message the report was lost at the process
// boundary, so an out-of-process plugin could not state a verdict and every
// failure it reported was retried as though transient.
